; 0089: a system call's number, read from a thread's context, cannot be
; written once for two CPUs. arm64 puts it in x8, word 8 of a context, and
; riscv64 in a7, which would be word 17; the stack pointer is word 31 on
; one and word 2 on the other. Nothing says which CPU this is, and the IR
; is the same for every host (spec section 9.2), so the compiler cannot
; choose either.
(def call_number ((c (array int))) int
  (array_get c 8))                        ; right on aarch64 alone

(def main () int
  (call_number (array_new 104 0)))
